course: dictionary
lesson: 13009
title: Putting out and ending
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Extinguishing means putting out a fire or a light so it stops burning. The root word is extinguish, and you will also see extinguishes and extinguished. «The firefighters worked hard at extinguishing the blaze.» The words firefighters and blaze are the clues: the fire was being put out.
explain: Extinguishing can also mean ending something completely, usually in a formal way. «The bad news was extinguishing all their hope.» Hope cannot burn, so the clue is that the hope was being wiped out. Ask yourself what would fit here, then try your meaning in the sentence to check it.
explain: Safety comes first. Never try extinguishing a big fire by yourself. Get out, stay out, and call for help. A fire extinguisher is only for an adult to use, and only when it is safe.
fact: Extinguishing means putting out a fire or a light so it stops burning.
fact: «Extinguishing the flames» means stopping the fire from burning.
fact: A fire goes out when it loses heat, fuel or oxygen.
fact: A fire extinguisher is a tool used to put out small fires.
fact: Formal use: «extinguishing all hope» means ending hope completely.
exercise: «The firefighters were busy extinguishing the blaze.» What does extinguishing mean here? | Running away from the smoke | *Putting out a fire so it stops burning | Lighting a new bonfire | Counting the fire engines
exercise: «Mia read the sign on the red fire extinguisher.» What is a fire extinguisher? | Ice cream sold at the beach | A kind of firework | A bucket for carrying sand to the park | *A tool used to put out fires
exercise: «The bad news was extinguishing all their hope.» What does extinguishing suggest? | Carrying hope to school | Making hope bright again | *Ending hope completely | Drawing a picture of hope
test: «The lights were extinguished at bedtime.» What does extinguished mean? | *Turned off so the light stopped shining | Turned on so the room glowed | Moved to the kitchen | Painted a bright colour
test: In science, what makes a fire go out? | Adding more wood to it | Making it windier | Shouting at it loudly | *Taking away heat, fuel or oxygen
exam: If a fire starts at home, what is the best rule? | Wait and see if it goes out by itself | Hide under the bed until it stops | *Get out, stay out, and call for help | Try extinguishing it alone with a bucket of water
